    "description": "Currently freelance software application development for various clients. I design, develop and publish android applications, perform frequent maintenance and bug fixes. I also am skilled at android application development and mentoring. I do not own apps ive developed but my work has been published. These android apps include an app to track voting for any end scene, an app to allow users to rate restaurants on cleanliness and search for a rated restaurant when dining out, and also a media player utilizing various codecs including matroska. I have experience using RESTful web services using JSON and XML processing, Realtime location tracking(GPS), Google Maps API and Google Places API with Multi-threading, Parcelable interface, and SQLite persistence. Additional technologies ive worked with includes Android, Java, Eclipse, REST, SQLite. I have a Ported 2D card game from Windows/.NET to Android/iOS: code ported from VB to C#, then into Unity.\nI have experimented with the following as well:Eclipse Plugin Development,UI Design and Development, Multi-threaded Java Application Development (mostly Open Source Application Development however), Wrote Developer Documents as per required by clients, and ive administered Subversion Repository as well.\nCurrently learning SOA and BPEL Application Development. Also learning DAO, and DTO Enhancement.",
